{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the J4 ordinary reader diff from V1 to V2, for request b5dc03f0. Verdict: APPROVED, for one later planner-executed ordinary read under a new Root release, and for nothing else.\n\nExact bytes:\n\n- Observer V2: PINS 0edc77bf, entry `observe-room.mjs` 19dbe154.\n- Capture V2: PINS 9c6dd69f, wrapper `run.py` 18373229.\n- Qualifier: receipt c0a71d19, report 534f8f47.\n\nBoth pin sets verify against their 28 and 20 files. This approval doesn't reuse 5c9f2934. It releases no setup, finalizer, admission or operator action.\n\n## The diff\n\n- The observer's only behavior changes remove `register` from the summary order, lower the expected requests to seven, add `reviewedRoom`, `observedScopes` and `unobservedScopes`, and replace the wording that overstated a failed result. Paths and digests move to V2.\n- The wrapper's only behavior change is the stricter `validate_observation`. Paths and digests move to V2, and the owner and the `Popen` seam are unchanged.\n- This meets my points 1 and 2 in c0fe8c4a. Register keeps its ref and pin as reviewed input, gains no observed head, and is named as unobserved.\n\n## Each route's authority, which my V1 review did not check\n\nI read these in the source at 112eff12:\n\n1. `GET /health` is public. It answered at 07:58 with version da13242c, and V1 got 200 on the live Worker.\n2. The session POST to Membership answered 200 on the live Worker in V1, per planner report 3bcf66ea.\n3. Directory, Membership, Rules and Destination summaries pass `checkSession` when the scope's own membership reference matches the token:\n   - `sessions.ts:246` uses the scope itself for Membership, and `config.membership` for the others;\n   - `directory.ts:425-429` supplies Directory's reference from `repository.refs.membership`;\n   - `authority.ts:400-438` resolves Rules and Destination through their actual Directory;\n   - `sessions.ts:285` requires `summary` in the token's reads for that Destination preparation, and `MEMBER_READS` at `sessions.ts:110` holds it.\n4. The Rules entry read needs `entry`, which `MEMBER_READS` also holds. The V14 operator makes the same read at `operator.mjs:231`.\n\nThe comment at `sessions.ts:245` says \"A register records no membership\", which confirms what I inferred in c0fe8c4a. Chained reads exclude summary, so Register was never readable this way.\n\nThe real-read evidence is the sealed V13 result, which ran these four summaries under the old deployment. `signed-reads.test.ts:407-460` reads the room's Destination, Rules and Directory with that room's session. I read that test's location from `ROUTE-EVIDENCE.md` and didn't rerun it. No read has yet shown these routes under Worker da13242c.\n\n## One gap I can't close\n\nThe planner said that the second S1 diagnostic recorded two summary 403s. I found them in `captures/r2-fork-state-diagnostic-1/stdout.log`, as observations 6 and 7. The rows carry categories only, so they don't name their scopes. `ROUTE-EVIDENCE.md` omits them for lack of a path. Those two refusals could be Register, or a scope in this list. I can't tell. If it's a scope in this list, V2 will refuse at that request and fail closed, as V1 did. I don't hold the approval for this, because the live read is the cheapest way to find out. Say which request refused if it does.\n\n## What I ran\n\n- I ran V2's `validate_observation` in a scratch copy on a value built from the real inputs, with the observer's exact qualification text taken from its source. It accepts the value. That value is built, not live, so this shows that the validator and the observer's output shape agree. It doesn't show that the room will answer.\n- The qualifier receipt closes 0/0 and complete, with source unchanged. Its report shows 7 of 7 cases passing and zero ambient fetches. HTTP, session and Membership answers are scripted, so this qualification can't see a refused route either, and it doesn't replace item 3 above.\n\n## Conditions for the run\n\nThe conditions in 5c9f2934 stand:\n\n1. Read this act back with `git show`, and bind it into the new Root release.\n2. Inspect `stderr.log` before sealing.\n3. Keep the private run directory out of evidence.\n4. Take no retry.\n5. Use the fresh V2 run directory, ready input and outputs, and don't touch the V1 capture.\n\n## Architecture\n\nRemoving one request leaves the design unchanged, and Register stays out of the observed set by name. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nThe read list shrinks and no authority is added: no signed read, history fallback or wider session. Approved, with the conditions above.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe change is the smallest that removes the refused route. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved, with the conditions above.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- This approval covers one later ordinary read of four scopes. It proves nothing about Register's current state, setup, providers, agent key possession, custody equality, Native Task or exports. Its outcome gets a separate review before any successor setup admission.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b2c392220092cabd459b92665284b9570723aec7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}